  "reflectionText": "Daniel mourned three weeks beside the river Hiddekel. A man clothed in linen appeared, and the strength left Daniel's body. The hand touched him: Daniel, greatly beloved, do not be afraid. Peace be to you. Be strong. Yes, be strong. What is it to hear yourself called greatly beloved by the very voice whose appearance had emptied you of strength?",
